# Token launch — one asset, spread across five holders.
#
# Amounts are written the way you read them: ORBIT has 2 decimals, so 10000
# below is ten thousand ORBIT and 2500 is two and a half thousand. The chain
# counts in hundredths underneath; the scenario does not make you do that.
#
# Issuing a token costs 150 SIGNA. That is why Treasury is funded with 4000
# and the holders, who only ever pay a transfer fee, with 200 each.

miner   Miner
account Treasury
account Ana
account Ben
account Cleo
account Dev

fund Treasury 4000
fund Ana 200
fund Ben 200
fund Cleo 200
fund Dev 200

info  Treasury "Orbit Labs" "Issuer of ORBIT"
token Treasury ORBIT 10000 2 "Governance token for the Orbit network"

# Most of the supply goes out, so the holdings are worth opening. Treasury
# keeps a fifth of it back.
transfer Treasury -> Ana  ORBIT 2500
transfer Treasury -> Ben  ORBIT 2000
transfer Treasury -> Cleo ORBIT 2000
transfer Treasury -> Dev  ORBIT 1500

# And a fraction, because a token with decimals should be seen using them.
transfer Ana -> Ben  ORBIT 125.5
transfer Ben -> Cleo ORBIT 62.25

alias Treasury orbit "Orbit Labs — ORBIT token"

forge 2
